  "body": "## What changed\n\nSlice A of #3514: the six slow tests of `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive_troch_tests.rs`.\n\n- The six full tests move into the new child module `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive_troch_heavy_tests.rs` (`mod heavy` of the `tests` module). Each full test has the ignore reason `heavy lane: motion heavy: lib (<s> s in debug, #3514)`.\n- Each full test keeps all its asserts and values. The only edit in a full body is the module path: `super::super::` becomes `super::super::super::`.\n- Each full test has a light twin `<full test>_light` in the same file. The light gate (`xtask/src/light.rs`) refuses a twin whose file has no ignored full test. Thus the twins and the full tests share one file.\n- `adaptive_troch_tests.rs` goes from 388 to 219 lines. The new file has 321 lines. No library code changes.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3514-motion-slow-tests.md`.\n\n## Readings (this machine, `-j 6`)\n\n| Test | Debug s, full (#3427) | Release s, full | Release s, twin | Reduced case of the twin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `the_pocket_face_is_cleared_inside_its_region_under_the_engagement_limit` | 76.2 | 4.21 | 3.04 | One level (bottom -3) of the 34x16 face in place of two. The same confinement, engagement, no-slot, clean-up note, rest < 20 mm2 and no-crossing asserts. |\n| `the_opened_bore_leaves_no_post_at_the_lane_start` | 139.8 | 8.12 | 2.99 | The production lane only: its opened bore leaves < 0.5 mm2. The plain-bore post and the stand-alone slot stay in the full test. |\n| `without_lift_room_the_returns_retract_and_a_plunge_entry_is_said_unread` | 72.5 (14.7 alone, see below) | 3.28 | 1.36 | The cut without lift room only (> 40 rapids, no feed above the clearance plane, the Entry note). The default-helix cross-check stays in the full test. |\n| `explicit_trochoidal_parameters_control_engagement_return_feed_and_loop_width` | 333.7 | 19.15 | 3.80 | A 16x12 face in place of 30x16. The three refusals by name and the custom lift with its 1800 return feed. The explicit Retract cut stays in the full test. The 10 deg refusal searches the face for its least engagement: 16.5 s on 30x16, 3.6 s on 16x12 (release). |\n| `custom_parameters_reach_parallel_and_closed_lane_layouts` | 332.2 | 4.26 | 2.34 | The 30x24 parallel layout only. The closed-lane ring stays in the full test. |\n| `custom_return_feed_is_emitted_by_production_parallel_lanes_and_cleanup` | 260.3 | 3.96 | 2.45 | A 24x20 pocket in place of 30x24. It still gives several lanes (the `lanes (` note), the 1800 return feed, the cutting feed and the confinement. |\n\n- No twin asserts a golden number. Each twin asserts the same law with the same limits as its full test.\n- Debug wall time of the default tests of the module after the move (`cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --lib machining2d::adaptive_troch::tests -- --test-threads=6`): 12 s (10 passed, 12 ignored).\n- Sanity check of the #3427 debug times: `without_lift_room_...` alone in debug takes 14.7 s, not 72.5 s. The #3427 times come from a parallel run of the whole crate, so they include contention. The release times above show the relative cost.\n- `#[test]` count of the module: 16 before, 22 after (+6 twins). No test is deleted.\n\n## Gates\n\n- Each moved full test ran one time in release by name (`cargo test -j 6 --release -p camcraft-motion --lib -- --ignored --exact <path>`): 6 passed. This is the targeted run of the moved tests, not the full heavy lane. The full heavy lane runs at the cut (AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\").\n- `cargo xtask gate light --dry-run`: `motion light: lib` lists the six new twins. `cargo xtask gate release --dry-run`: `motion heavy: lib` runs all ignored lib tests.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6 cargo xtask gate light --only \"motion light: lib\"`: ok in 12 s, 7 passed (the six new twins and `the_slot_keeps_its_verdict_under_sub_micron_perturbations_light`).\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --lib --profile test -- -D warnings`: clean. No integration binary changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full heavy lane `motion heavy: lib` (cut only).\n- Slices B and C of #3514 (`adaptive/tests.rs`, `pocket_hsm_ring.rs`, and the three `tests/adaptive_troch_*.rs` binaries).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #3514\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
